# perceived_by_sense: P1 is plausible only if "things we perceive by sense" includes objects we perceive by way of sensations.
# P2 is plausible only if it means what is directly before the mind in sensing.
# This is the standard charge against this argument, though Berkeley himself would deny there is a second sense.
